---
// Invariant C, shape #5: Supabase's newer name for the same thing.
//
// `service_role` is the legacy JWT-based key; the current key scheme calls the privileged
// half the SECRET key, and its environment variable is spelled accordingly. Both are in
// circulation — the dashboard, the docs and half the tutorials on the internet disagree
// about which to show — so a rule that knew only one of them would go green the day this
// project adopted the other, with nothing anywhere to indicate that anything had changed.
//
// That is the failure mode a name-bound rule has, and it is silent. This page is what
// keeps the newer spelling from being the one that gets through.
const secretKey = import.meta.env.SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY;
---

<p>{secretKey ? 'configured' : 'absent'}</p>
